cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Ion-Pot in your research, please cite both the paper and
  this software release.
title: "Ion-Pot: Voxel-based CNN surrogates for ion-dependent biomolecular electrostatic potential prediction"
abstract: >-
  Ion-Pot is a voxel-based learning benchmark and set of CNN surrogates
  for predicting the electrostatic potential field around biomolecules
  under varying ionic conditions. Given a voxelized representation of a
  protein and a scalar salt concentration, the models predict the full
  3D electrostatic potential that would otherwise be computed by a
  nonlinear Poisson–Boltzmann solver (APBS). This repository contains
  the dataset construction pipeline (AlphaFoldDB source, 3,875 proteins
  × 9 ionic conditions), voxel data loaders, U-Net / ResNet / FNO
  backbones with additive or FiLM ion-concentration conditioning,
  distributed training, and APBS benchmarking utilities.
